{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_34bynfgxzmorx44avgbz6hny7nkaeacemrlwgkqim5lqsllm7zma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 93 tests pass. The translation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Phase 1 — Translation:** Implemented all `unimplemented!()` bodies in `src/simple_config.rs`, including:\n- `cfg_parse` and `cfg_parse_file` — full byte-level scanner that mirrors the C parser, including ASCII-only ctype semantics, error tracking with row/col, integer/float overflow checks, and proper handling of strings, bools, ints, floats, and rgba colors.\n- `cfg_get_*` family — searches entries in reverse (last-wins, matching C) and falls back when the key is missing or the value type doesn't match.\n- `cfg_get_*_min/max/range` — wrap the basic getters and apply C's range-check fallback semantics.\n- `Display` impls for `CfgError`, `CfgColor`, `CfgVal`, `CfgEntry`, `Cfg` — formats match C's `fprintf` output (e.g. `%f` → 6 decimals, `rgba(r, g, b, a)`, `Error at row:col :: msg\\n`).\n- `cfg_fprint` and `cfg_fprint_error` — write the `Display` output to a `File`.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no extra dependencies — pure safe Rust.\n\n**Phase 2 — Tests:** Compiled the C reference (`gcc example.c config.c`) and a probe program, captured ground-truth values, then wrote 93 tests in `src/bin/test_simple_config.rs` covering:\n- Successful parsing (empty, whitespace, comments, all value types, multiple entries, rgba edge cases including alpha rounding).\n- Every parse error from the C test suite, asserting `msg`, `off`, `row`, and `col` against the C-derived values.\n- All `cfg_get_*` functions with present/missing/wrong-type/range-violating inputs.\n- `cfg_parse_file` for short filenames, wrong extensions, missing files, and a real `.cfg` round-trip.\n- `Display` impls for every type (including the exact print output from `c_src/test/test_print.c`).\n- Constants, `From` conversions, and `CfgError::default`.\n\n`carg